{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"tests/e2e/_toolchain.py","reason":"new: provision_toolchain() with explicit per-step timeout=, a step-naming ToolchainProvisioningError, and a cross-process lock so concurrent xdist workers cannot race the same node_modules/dist"},{"path":"tests/e2e/conftest.py","reason":"bpmn_harness delegates provisioning to _toolchain and converts its named error into the tier's existing self-skip instead of running two unbounded subprocesses inside a test's 300s pytest-timeout budget"},{"path":"tests/e2e/test_toolchain_provisioning.py","reason":"new: deterministic stub-npm tests for the stalled-install and stalled-build named failures, the concurrency serialization, and the Makefile/workflow build-ordering assertions"},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"portable e2e-deps target (npm ci + npm run build in tests/e2e/js) so the fix is not CI-only per project.portability"},{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"npm cache keyed on tests/e2e/js/package-lock.json plus a make e2e-deps step before the pytest step, so cold install time is not charged against a single test's timeout budget"}]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1788480725098988001,"uuid":"7fa1957c-908e-40f4-a6dc-cfdecf1bd95a"}